  "metric": "GPU on-device memory bandwidth",
  "unit": "GB/s",
  "definition": "Peak data-transfer rate between a GPU and its own attached memory, in decimal gigabytes per second (10^9 bytes/s). This is distinct from network, PCIe and NVLink bandwidth.",
  "modelInput": "bandwidthPerGpuGBps: use the per-device value together with a separate GPU count. gpuMemoryBandwidthGBps is only the sum of installed, separate per-device capacities.",
  "sourcePolicy": "Join exact publicly documented cloud GPU hardware to a primary manufacturer or provider peak specification. Keep variant-specific PCIe/SXM and memory-capacity distinctions. No imputation for missing or ambiguous variants.",
  "limitations": [
    "Peak hardware bandwidth is not measured cloud VM bandwidth or application throughput. Cloud clocks and power limits may differ.",
    "The sum across devices is not a unified memory pool or an application scaling guarantee.",
    "Fractional, partitioned, shared, heterogeneous, unknown and conflicting GPU mappings are excluded.",
    "GPU specifications are reviewed separately from daily prices. Their retrievedAt dates are not advanced by price refreshes.",
    "hardwareMemoryPerGpuGB is a hardware nominal source annotation, not a replacement for the catalog provider capacity or an assertion about usable bytes."
  ],
